faqs:
  - q: "How does the Days Until Date Calculator work?"
    a: "The calculator computes the exact calendar distance between today's date and your selected target date. All date math is performed using UTC midnight timestamps to eliminate daylight saving time (DST) shifts that often cause off-by-one errors on other calculators."
  - q: "Does this calculator take leap years into account?"
    a: "Yes. The algorithm fully accounts for 366-day leap years (including February 29th) when computing spans across calendar years."
  - q: "Can I calculate how many days have passed since a past date?"
    a: "Yes. If you pick a date in the past, the tool automatically detects it and displays the elapsed time in days, weeks, and months since that date."
  - q: "How are months and days broken down?"
    a: "Months are calculated from full calendar month transitions. The remaining days are clamped to the exact length of the preceding month, correctly handling months with 28, 29, 30, or 31 days."
  - q: "Is my input date stored or sent to a server?"
    a: "No. All calculation logic runs strictly inside your web browser using standard JavaScript. No personal dates or event names leave your device."
  - q: "Does the countdown update dynamically if I leave the page open?"
    a: "The calculation runs whenever you select a date or reload the page. For real-time updates at midnight, refresh the page to update the base date."
  - q: "Can I use this calculator for wedding or retirement planning?"
    a: "Yes. Enter your future retirement or wedding date to view the remaining time broken down into total days, weeks, and calendar months."
